// doc-in-float-demo — a float whose body is itself a small document built with the document package.
//
// This stresses the paragraph-indentation rules from every side at once. The outer document indents normally: the
// first paragraph after each heading is flush, the ones after it are indented. The figure floats a whole little
// document, set a couple of sizes smaller, with its own title and two headings — and inside it the same rules must
// hold: the paragraph that opens a heading is flush, the next is indented. Finally the text after the float must be
// untouched by the headings nested in it: a detached float never flushes the paragraph that follows it. The float's
// sections use the starred \section* so the inner document does not disturb the outer document's section numbering.

\use{document}
\use{float}

\title {A Float Containing a Document}
\author {the float package}
\maketitle

\section{An ordinary section}

This first paragraph opens the section, so it is set flush to the left margin. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet,
consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim
veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat.

This second paragraph follows the first, so it takes the usual first-line indent. Duis aute irure dolor in
reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur, excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non
proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum.

\figure{
  {\footnotesize
    \centerline{\font lmroman 11 bold A Tiny Document}
    \vskip 1pt
    \centerline{a whole document, floated}
    \vskip 8pt

    \section*{First Section}
    The first paragraph after this heading is flush, just as in the outer document. Sed ut perspiciatis unde omnis
    iste natus error sit voluptatem accusantium doloremque laudantium, totam rem aperiam.

    The second paragraph is indented. Eaque ipsa quae ab illo inventore veritatis et quasi architecto beatae vitae
    dicta sunt explicabo, nemo enim ipsam voluptatem quia voluptas sit aspernatur.

    \section*{Second Section}
    This section has a single paragraph, flush because it opens the section. Neque porro quisquam est, qui dolorem
    ipsum quia dolor sit amet, consectetur, adipisci velit.
  }
  \caption{A small document, set in a float and floated to the top of the page.}
}

The text after the float resumes here, and its indentation is untouched by the document nested in the float: this
paragraph is indented because it follows the one before it, not flushed by the float's internal headings. At vero
eos et accusamus et iusto odio dignissimos ducimus qui blanditiis praesentium voluptatum deleniti atque corrupti.

\section{A second outer section}

The first paragraph here is flush again, opening the section. Itaque earum rerum hic tenetur a sapiente delectus,
ut aut reiciendis voluptatibus maiores alias consequatur aut perferendis doloribus asperiores repellat.

And a second, indented paragraph closes the demonstration. Nam libero tempore, cum soluta nobis est eligendi optio
cumque nihil impedit quo minus id quod maxime placeat facere possimus, omnis voluptas assumenda est.
